487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (Low-code application development is emerging as an important approach to modern software development. The technology is evolving beyond simple drag-and-drop application creation toward an ecosystem involving AI, Generative AI, automation, cloud computing, analytics, APIs, IoT, and citizen development.)
/E (Low-code application development is emerging as an important approach to modern software development. The technology is evolving beyond simple drag-and-drop application creation toward an ecosystem involving AI, Generative AI, automation, cloud computing, analytics, APIs, IoT, and citizen development.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (The available market data indicates strong growth in enterprise adoption. Gartner's prediction that 70% of new enterprise applications would use low-code or no-code technologies by 2025 demonstrates the growing importance of this approach.)
/E (The available market data indicates strong growth in enterprise adoption. Gartner's prediction that 70% of new enterprise applications would use low-code or no-code technologies by 2025 demonstrates the growing importance of this approach.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (The most significant future trend is likely to be AI-powered low-code development, where users can describe application requirements in natural language and receive AI-assisted application designs, workflows, code, and analytics.)
/E (The most significant future trend is likely to be AI-powered low-code development, where users can describe application requirements in natural language and receive AI-assisted application designs, workflows, code, and analytics.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (However, organizations must address security, governance, scalability, data privacy, and vendor lock-in. Therefore, the future of application development is unlikely to be purely low-code or purely traditional. Instead, a hybrid model combining professional developers, citizen developers, low-code platforms, and AI is likely to become increasingly important.)
/E (However, organizations must address security, governance, scalability, data privacy, and vendor lock-in. Therefore, the future of application development is unlikely to be purely low-code or purely traditional. Instead, a hybrid model combining professional developers, citizen developers, low-code platforms, and AI is likely to become increasingly important.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
